**Phase 2 — Branch.** Reverse scan from each deref: for `render` (line 6 producer → uses at 9ff) and `next` (line 32 producer → use line 34) the only backward statements are `assert(render)` (line 7) and `assert(next)` (line 33), which DO-NOT-CREDIT removes; no shown statement inside the fragment assigns NULL or demonstrably yields a NULL `data[0]` for these member lookups, so per the NULL-producer rule (plain member pointers are non-NULL unless a shown statement makes them NULL) these are limitations, not findings. For `last`: producer line 37 → `if (!last) last = render;` (lines 38–39) executes on every reaching path before `last->surface` (line 40); guard identity holds (same value `last`, no modification between check and use); admitted set after the guard is non-NULL. `switch(s->pict_type)` (line 30) is a dispatch, not a security decision; the `FF_B_TYPE`→`FF_P_TYPE` fall-through sets both references without memory-safety impact. `if (slice_count)` (line 44) excludes 0 from the `ff_draw_horiz_band` call.

**Phase 3 — Loop.** `for (i = 0; i < 64; ++i)` (line 24) yields `i ∈ 0..63`, terminates, and `i` reaches lines 25–26. However, no declaration or allocation of `intra_quantizer_matrix`, `non_intra_quantizer_matrix`, `intra_matrix`, or `inter_matrix` is shown, so CAPACITY-EVIDENCE RULE demotes any OOB claim in both directions — no quoted capacity, no witness.

**Phase 4 — Per-sink Fix-Presence and tests.** (i) `render` derefs: ABSENT-as-finding demoted — no shown NULL producer (assert not credited); limitation. (ii) `next->surface`: same, limitation. (iii) `last->surface`: PRESENT — `if (!last) last = render;` quoted at lines 38–39, excluded set `{NULL}`, degenerate input `last==NULL` is replaced, reach covers all paths; BREAK test passes; only residual (unshown) risk is `render` itself being NULL, which no shown statement produces. (iv) loop copies: no confirmable failure set without capacities; limitation. (v) `ff_vdpau_add_data_chunk`: callee body and buffer capacities unshown, `buf_size` failure set unconfirmable; limitation. (vi) `ff_draw_horiz_band`: guarded for `slice_count==0`; other failure modes live in an unshown callee; limitation. BLOCK test: no claimed witness survives because no ABSENT sink has a produced failing value. Verdict: NOT VULNERABLE — no dangerous operation resolves ABSENT with a surviving witness; decisive guard is the `last` NULL replacement, and the remainder collapse to unshown-capacity/NULL-producer limitations, so confidence stays in the ≤0.55 band.

