A protective statement that fails any of the four does not resolve its sink PRESENT;re-classify that sink ABSENTwith the surviving witness.



THE BLOCK TEST(mandatory for every claimed failing witness before a VULNERABLE verdict,:walk the witness from its producer to the sink, one shown statement at a time,and at each step ask whether any shown statement excludes the value or blocks the path(a check, an early return, an initialization, a cast's truncation,a bounded copy,. If any step is blocked,the witness dies—the verdict must be withdrawn orthe witness replaced. The surviving witness must be admitted by every guard in execution order, reach the sink without further modification,and be derivable from the fragment alone(or from a callee's standard semantics,. A witness that depends on unshown environmental facts,on an out-of-scope caller violating an API contract,or on a producer the fragment cannot drive is invalid;record the mechanism in `notes.limitations` instead。. INDEPENDENT-SINK SWEEP(mandatory:once one sink resolves PRESENT, do NOT stop： RE-RUN every inventoried dangerous operation through the same PRESENT/ABSENT test. A protective statement protects ONLY the sink it guards: a second copy, a second dereference, a second index, a second branch, or a second untracked status use can carry its own unguarded failure. The verdict is the CONJUNCTION across ALL inventoried operations:any single ABSENT resolution with a surviving witness ⇒ VULNERABLE, even when another sink is perfectly guarded.



